Revision history for IO-K8s

{{$NEXT}}

  - IO::K8s::AutoGen types inline objects (D10, k94). A type: object
    with properties -- which is how every CRD schema is written below its
    top level -- now becomes a nested class named after its place in the
    parent (<Kind>::Spec, <Kind>::Spec::Limit, ...Item for array items,
    ...Value for map values) instead of an opaque hash, so field options,
    strict and the unknown-field bag reach every level. Hash-style access
    on such a field keeps working (a Moo object is a blessed hash);
    property-less objects and additionalProperties-only maps stay opaque.
    A direct Class->new(spec => { ... }) on such a generated class now
    fails its type constraint (a plain hashref no longer satisfies an
    object-typed field); inflate/new_object/FROM_HASH still coerce a
    hashref into the right nested class as before. This applies to any
    AutoGen class with a typed nested object, including one built from a
    live cluster's /openapi/v2, not only to a class IO::K8s::CRD generated
    from a CRD manifest. IO::K8s::AutoGen::class_description / class_path
    / class_root are new public functions (used by IO::K8s::CRD::Emitter
    below). IO::K8s::Resource::_sanitize_attr_name now maps every
    character outside [A-Za-z0-9_] to '_', not only '-', '.' and '/': a
    property key with any other odd character becomes an attribute
    instead of dying at class load.

  - New IO::K8s::CRD and IO::K8s->add_crd (D10, k94): load a
    CustomResourceDefinition (object, hashref, YAML/JSON text, path, or a
    list of those), generate one class per served version, register every
    version under its domain-qualified key and the storage version under
    the bare Kind -- through add(), so a provider merged earlier keeps the
    short name. Generated classes live under a "::_CRD" sub-namespace of
    the instance's own AutoGen namespace, never the bare namespace itself:
    without it, a CRD manifest and an openapi_spec definition for the same
    GVK would build the identical class name and alias in AutoGen's
    per-class-name cache, silently discarding whichever generated second
    while add_crd still reported success. Two CRDs that share a bare Kind
    across groups now merge under that Kind in add_crd's return value
    (every version from both present, storage kept from the FIRST
    registration) instead of the second overwriting the first outright.

  - New IO::K8s::CRD::Emitter renders generated classes as house-style
    source files from the attribute registry (fields, options, required,
    descriptions as =attr POD, a name map for upstream Go type names).
    maint/crd-drift-check.pl --suggest prints those files for every
    OPAQUE SPEC / MISSING FIELD Kind; --suggest-dir writes them, and
    refuses a directory inside lib/. A pattern, enum member or default
    carrying a character above ASCII (Traefik's "^[0-9]+\xB5s$", say)
    renders as a \x{HEX}-escaped, ASCII-only Perl literal rather than the
    raw character, which used to interpolate straight into the file and
    silently reject a value the generated class accepted; a schema
    description carrying such a character stays verbatim in POD, and the
    file gains "use utf8;" plus "=encoding UTF-8" only when it needs to.

  - maint/crd-drift-check.pl decodes a fetched manifest as UTF-8 once,
    before caching it, instead of writing the raw response bytes through
    an ':encoding(UTF-8)' filehandle -- doing that to undecoded bytes
    double-encoded every non-ASCII character on disk (Traefik's "µs"
    became four garbled bytes in the cache). A cache file written before
    this fix is detected and corrected on read rather than needing to be
    deleted. --suggest's rendered source (and --suggest-dir's "wrote N
    file(s)" confirmation) now goes to stderr instead of stdout when
    --format json is active, so stdout stays one parseable JSON document.

  - IO::K8s::AutoGen caps a path-derived nested class name at 200
    characters instead of risking "Identifier too long": cert-manager's
    CRDs inline a full PodTemplateSpec several levels into a
    ClusterIssuer/Challenge spec, and the resulting name ran past Perl's
    251-character limit on a fully qualified identifier, which made
    IO::K8s::CRD->generate -- and maint/crd-drift-check.pl --suggest --
    fail closed for all three affected Kinds. A name that would exceed
    the cap is replaced with <root>::_<10 hex chars> (a SHA-1 of the full
    logical name); the logical path survives the shortening and is
    recoverable via the new IO::K8s::AutoGen::class_path / class_root.
    IO::K8s::CRD::Emitter renders such a class from that recovered path
    rather than from its own (possibly hashed) name, so the emitted
    source usually keeps the readable package name even where AutoGen's
    own namespace-qualified one had to be hashed; only when the emitted
    name would itself exceed 200 characters, or a long "base" would push
    the full joined package name past 255, does it fall back the same
    way, and a names entry still overrides either.

  - IO::K8s::AutoGen checks x-kubernetes-int-or-string before the type
    dispatch (k94). A property that marks Kubernetes' IntOrString union
    this way and carries no type of its own -- the structural-schema
    convention -- previously fell through to Str; found while building
    IO::K8s::CRD::Emitter, whose registry-type assertion is stricter than
    a Str field's own round-trip. A malformed value there is treated as
    false (falls through to the ordinary type-based dispatch) rather than
    aborting class generation.

  - The k8s DSL takes per-field options (D3 of the CRD design, k93):
    k8s replicas => Int, { minimum => 0, maximum => 10, default => 1 },
    or name => [ Type, { ... } ] inside an inline struct. required,
    default, enum, minimum, maximum, pattern, description, nullable and
    preserve_unknown are recorded in the attribute registry for the CRD
    schema that to_crd will emit; enum, minimum, maximum and pattern are
    also enforced at construction on scalar fields, arrays of scalars and
    typed value maps, failing with "Value "x" is not one of: ...", "is
    below the minimum N" / "is above the maximum N" and "does not match
    the pattern ...". default is never applied client-side. required => 1
    both enforces and records, like the legacy 'required' marker and the
    Type! suffix; required => 'schema' records required => 1 without
    enforcing it, for a field a real document may validly omit. An option
    a field cannot carry (enum on Bool, minimum on Str, pattern on an
    object) is a class-load error naming class and field -- as is a type
    spec _k8s cannot interpret at all (a Type::Tiny outside the seven
    kinds, or a coderef), which now croaks "k8s: cannot interpret the
    type of field ..." instead of silently building an unconstrained
    attribute.

  - IO::K8s::AutoGen carries an OpenAPI property's required list, enum,
    minimum, maximum, pattern, default, description, nullable and
    x-kubernetes-preserve-unknown-fields into those options, per element
    for arrays, so a generated class enforces a bad enum/range/pattern
    value at construction exactly like a hand-written one does. The
    schema's required list becomes required => 'schema': recorded (for
    to_crd) but not enforced, since a real cluster document can validly
    omit a field the schema requires -- a server-side default, or a
    status object not yet populated -- and inflate must not die over
    that. A malformed schema option -- a minimum above the maximum or a
    non-numeric bound, a default the field cannot hold, an enum
    containing a JSON null -- is dropped the same way an uncompilable
    pattern already was, rather than failing class generation.

  - Unknown fields are kept instead of dropped (D1 of the CRD design,
    docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-03-crd-design.md). A constructor key no
    attribute claims -- on inflate, new_object, FROM_HASH or a direct
    ->new, at any nesting level including inline structs -- now lands in
    the object's _unknown_fields bag and TO_JSON emits it again, declared
    attributes winning on a clash. Before, every class silently lost such
    a field on the round-trip (the README AgentSandbox example passed a
    spec.replicas that vanished, k91). IO::K8s->new(strict => 1) makes
    the same situation die with "Unknown field '<name>' for <class>" for
    the duration of that instance's inflate / new_object / json_to_object
    / struct_to_object calls (load and load_yaml inherit it).

  - SpecBuilder walks typed specs (k90). spec_get/spec_set/spec_push/
    spec_merge/spec_delete used to assume spec was a plain hashref; on a
    class whose spec is an inline struct (the eight AgentSandbox classes)
    spec_set replaced the struct with an empty hash and wrote into an
    orphan, so to_json emitted spec: {} afterwards. The methods now walk
    objects through their accessors, vivify missing intermediates as the
    declared class, inflate hashrefs handed to typed slots, and put a key
    an object does not declare into its _unknown_fields bag. A -1 path
    segment addresses the last array element, or a freshly created one on
    an empty array. New: spec_array($path) and spec_hash($path) return
    the vivified container. The builder roles (CertManaged, HelmManaged,
    MiddlewareBuilder, Loadbalanced, Routable's gateway and traefik
    branches, NetworkPolicy's cilium branch) are expressed in these calls
    and therefore work on hash and object specs alike. Visible changes:
    Routable::add_path_match on a traefik route with an unknown type no
    longer leaves an empty route behind; on a plain-hash spec too,
    spec_push onto a path holding a defined non-array value now croaks
    instead of replacing it, spec_set through a defined scalar
    intermediate croaks instead of clobbering it, and spec_set('a.5', ...)
    on an empty array croaks instead of autovivifying the holes in
    between. Every failure raised while walking or vivifying begins with
    the spec path and carries no internal file/line (k101); a class with
    required attributes cannot be vivified, since it would have to be
    constructed with none.

  - README: the AgentSandbox example no longer passes spec.replicas, a
    field neither the class nor upstream agent-sandbox v1.0.0 has (k91).

  - Bump CRD-provider upstream pins (k85-k88). Verified with
    maint/crd-drift-check.pl against each new upstream release:
      * Cilium v1.20.0 -> v1.20.1 (k85) -- no schema drift.
      * Traefik v3.7.10 -> v3.7.12 (k86) -- no schema drift.
      * K3s v1.36.3+k3s1 -> v1.36.4+k3s1 (k87) -- schemaless upstream;
        version pin only (k3s has no v1.37 release yet).
      * AgentSandbox v0.5.4 -> v1.0.0 (k88) -- v1.0.0 removes the entire
        v1alpha1 track upstream (all four Kinds now serve v1beta1 only).
        The four v1alpha1 classes are kept as a back-compat superset for
        clusters still on agent-sandbox v0.5.x and suppressed via new
        ignore_stale_kinds entries in maint/crd-drift-exceptions.yaml; the
        v1beta1 classes still match upstream exactly.
    GatewayAPI (v1.6.1) and CertManager (v1.21.1) were already current.

  - Register the missing cilium.io/v2alpha1/CiliumLoadBalancerIPPool
    back-compat GVK (k83). Upstream Cilium v1.20 serves
    CiliumLoadBalancerIPPool at both cilium.io/v2 and cilium.io/v2alpha1,
    but the k78 back-compat pass covered only the sibling BGP/CIDR Kinds --
    the v2alpha1 LB pool had no shipped class and did not inflate. A new
    opaque IO::K8s::Cilium::V2alpha1::CiliumLoadBalancerIPPool class is
    registered under its domain-qualified key, mirroring k78; the
    CiliumLoadBalancerIPPool short name still resolves to the v2 storage
    version.

  - Drop spec.volumeClaimTemplatesPolicy from
    IO::K8s::AgentSandbox::V1alpha1::SandboxTemplate (k84). Upstream
    agent-sandbox v0.5.4 adds that field only at v1beta1; the v1alpha1 CRD
    schema does not carry it, so the shipped v1alpha1 class over-modelled by
    one field. The v1beta1 class keeps the field; POD on both tracks is
    corrected.

  - New maintenance tool maint/crd-drift-check.pl (k82): the CRD-provider
    analog of spec-drift-check.pl. It fetches each provider's upstream CRD
    manifests at its declared upstream_version, parses the openAPIV3Schema
    and reports missing Kinds, missing/extra spec fields and stale classes
    against the shipped resource_map and class registries. Each provider
    gains a data-only crd_sources hook beside upstream_version; deliberate
    non-gaps live in maint/crd-drift-exceptions.yaml. Report-only -- it
    never edits lib/ and never creates tickets. K3s reports its source as
    unresolved (k3s ships schemaless wrangler CRDs upstream).

  - Make the eight back-compat Cilium classes restored in 1.105 actually
    reachable (k78). The v2alpha1 BGP/CIDR tracks
    (CiliumBGPAdvertisement, CiliumBGPClusterConfig, CiliumBGPNodeConfig,
    CiliumBGPNodeConfigOverride, CiliumBGPPeerConfig, CiliumCIDRGroup),
    CiliumBGPPeeringPolicy (v2alpha1) and CiliumExternalWorkload (v2)
    loaded as classes but were absent from IO::K8s::Cilium's resource_map,
    so inflate()/new_object() on their GVKs died "Cannot resolve
    Kubernetes GVK" -- the stated purpose (serving clusters on older
    Cilium releases) did not work. They are now registered under
    domain-qualified keys, mirroring the k58 AgentSandbox pattern, so the
    v2 short names keep resolving to the storage version.

  - Fix the built META.json x_authority, which read "cpan:cpan:JLMARTIN"
    (k75). dist.ini carried authority = cpan:JLMARTIN, but the
    Author::GETTY plugin bundle prepends "cpan:" itself; the doubled
    prefix -- shipped in every release to date -- did not match
    cpan:JLMARTIN, so authority-aware tooling could not confirm the
    co-maintainer's claim. dist.ini now carries the bare PAUSE id.

  - Documentation corrections for the 1.108 audit: README and the core
    POD now say Kubernetes v1.37 (k74, k79); the per-Kind API-class doc
    reference URLs were moved from v1.36 to v1.37 to match (k74); the
    dangling L</TO_JSON> / L</to_json> links in Role::Resource are
    resolved and the serialization entry points documented (k76); the
    fail-closed kind()/api_version()/resource_plural() and new_object
    apiVersion contracts are now stated in POD (k79); and the builder
    roles and IO::K8s::Types::Net ship with full =method/=func POD (k80).

  - Track upstream Kubernetes v1.37: 22 new Kinds (among them a new
    IO::K8s::Api::Lifecycle namespace), their supporting types and new
    fields, all registered for GVK dispatch (k72).

  - Ten fields upstream made required in v1.37 are now required at
    construction (k72): the apps/v1 workload specs, ControllerRevision
    .data, and five flowcontrol/v1 fields. Building one without the field
    now dies instead of yielding a partial object.

  - resource_plural() now croaks when passed an argument instead of silently
    swallowing it, in all three spots (role accessor, APIObject import param,
    AutoGen GVK constant) -- the same fail-closed shape k67 applied to
    kind()/api_version() (k70)
  - The k8s DSL gains a hash-of-scalar-type form, { Quantity => 1 } (and
    Int/Num/Bool/Time/IntOrStr), and the fields upstream declares as
    map[ResourceName]Quantity are retyped onto it (k63). Those maps
    -- ResourceRequirements and VolumeResourceRequirements limits/requests,
    NodeStatus capacity/allocatable, ResourceQuota hard/used, LimitRangeItem
    max/min/default/defaultRequest/maxLimitRequestRatio, PersistentVolume(Claim)
    capacity and allocatedResources, and the DRA capacity/requests fields --
    validated nothing: limits => { cpu => 'banana' } constructed happily and
    only failed at the API server. Each value is now type-checked at
    construction. The bare { Str => 1 } form stays deliberately opaque for
    genuinely free-form maps (labels, annotations, fieldsV1, and
    PersistentVolumeClaimStatus allocatedResourceStatuses, whose values are
    a status enum, not a Quantity).

  - The k8s DSL gains array-of-hash and array-of-array forms, [ {} ] and
    [ [] ], and AutoGen maps items: object / items: array onto them
    (k66). Both used to fall through to [ Str ], so a generated class
    rejected the very hashrefs and arrayrefs the schema describes on an
    ArrayRef[Str] constraint that never named the real problem. The
    contents are opaque -- validated as the right container shape,
    otherwise passed through with the same one-level copy a free-form
    HashRef gets.

  - The k8s DSL gains a Num scalar type, and AutoGen maps OpenAPI
    type: number onto it instead of Str (k68). A JSON number in a
    generated class used to round-trip as a quoted string ({"cpu":1.5}
    came back {"cpu":"1.5"}), which the API server rejects for a numeric
    field. Num serializes unquoted, the fractional counterpart to Int's
    int-cast; Quantity remains a string type, unchanged.

  - IO::K8s::List gains from_json, so serializing a List and reading it
    back no longer dies with "Can not locate object method from_json"
    (k64) -- it was the last class outside the to_json/from_json
    symmetry k59 established. List is a container, not a
    Role::Resource, so from_json is hand-rolled and delegates to
    FROM_STRUCT (an optional IO::K8s instance as the second argument lets
    item types resolve through your providers). List->to_json now also
    emits a UTF-8 byte string like every other class, instead of a
    wide-character string that round-tripped non-ASCII data to mojibake
    (the k53 convention). ASCII payloads are unaffected.

  - new_object() now honours an apiVersion passed inside the params hash,
    the same key inflate() already reads, instead of silently resolving
    the short name to its default version (k62). It used to take the
    exact-GVK request only as its third positional argument, so
    new_object('Sandbox', { apiVersion => '.../v1alpha1' }) built a
    v1beta1 object with no diagnostic -- a version the caller never asked
    for. Behaviour change: an apiVersion in the params hash that cannot be
    resolved now fails closed, and one that contradicts an explicit
    positional api_version croaks rather than picking one.

  - kind() and api_version() now croak when passed an argument instead of
    silently ignoring it (k67). They are derived, read-only identity
    accessors; the swallow meant a caller who wrote $obj->kind('Other')
    believing they had retargeted the object got no error and no change,
    and only found out at the API server, if at all. Behaviour change on
    the two most-called accessors: this covers the hand-written classes
    (via IO::K8s::Role::APIObject), CRD classes declaring api_version as
    an import parameter, and AutoGen-generated GVK classes. The
    no-argument reads are unchanged.

  - add() no longer re-qualifies a provider resource_map key that is
    already domain-qualified (k61). A key carrying a '/' is an exact
    GVK request registered verbatim; merging IO::K8s::GatewayAPI or
    IO::K8s::AgentSandbox used to also produce junk
    "$group/$version/$group/$version/$Kind" keys that nothing could
    resolve. Harmless at lookup time, but they polluted resource_map for
    anyone iterating or counting it.

  - FROM_HASH now inflates nested objects, so every class is to_json /
    from_json symmetric (k59). Pod->from_json($pod->to_json) used to
    die at the first object-typed field with a bare Moo type error on
    metadata that never pointed at the path which worked
    ($k8s->json_to_object). Behaviour change: FROM_HASH used to be the
    shallow entry point and raw nested hashrefs were refused. It also
    inherits the k42 diagnostics now, and an explicit undef on a
    required Bool dies with "Missing required arguments" instead of
    building the object -- that is a convergence, $k8s->struct_to_object
    already behaved that way. IO::K8s::List does not consume the role and
    still has no from_json.

  - from_json now decodes UTF-8, symmetric to to_json (k53).
    Class->from_json($obj->to_json) read the encoded bytes as characters
    and produced mojibake with no error raised -- silent data mutation on
    the class-level round-trip. Behaviour change: from_json takes a UTF-8
    encoded byte string, which is exactly what to_json emits. An already
    decoded character string is no longer accepted silently; it fails
    loudly. Pure ASCII is unaffected. A tolerance shim was rejected
    deliberately: it would have made from_json more permissive than
    $k8s->json_to_object, which has always been byte-oriented.

  - TO_JSON and the inflation path no longer share array and hash
    references with the object (k54). Post-processing the struct from
    TO_JSON silently mutated the object and the mutation showed up in
    every later serialization: $cm->TO_JSON->{data}{key} = "MUTATED"
    changed $cm->data->{key}. Mutating a source struct after
    $k8s->inflate reached the object the same way. Both directions now
    shallow-copy. The depth is deliberately one level: structures nested
    under an opaque hash attribute (fieldsV1 and friends) still share
    their inner references.

  - An undef element in an array of Bool now dies instead of being
    serialized as false (k51). bools => [1, undef, 0] emitted
    {"bools":[true,false,false]} -- the same invented-false problem
    k48 fixed one level up, where omitting the field is not an option
    because the positions would shift. The message names class, field and
    element index. The element still passes the constructor (Bool
    includes undef); the refusal happens at the wire boundary. Affects
    DeviceAttribute bools, which upstream documents as a non-empty list
    of true/false values.

  - Quantity now accepts the n (nano) and u (micro) decimal SI suffixes
    (k52). "100n" was rejected, so inflating real cluster data failed
    on the 30 Quantity-typed fields -- metrics-server reports CPU that way
    and autoscaling/v2 averageValue carries such values. The suffix set
    now matches the decimal table in upstream suffix.go exactly. Note the
    BNF in the doc comment of upstream quantity.go is stale and omits
    both suffixes. Quantities without a digit in the mantissa ("Ki", "m",
    ".") stay rejected although upstream parses them as 0; no component
    emits them and accepting them would swallow a typo.

  - AgentSandbox v1alpha1 kinds are reachable by domain-qualified name
    (k58). agents.x-k8s.io/v1alpha1/Sandbox and the three
    extensions.agents.x-k8s.io/v1alpha1 kinds resolved to undef and died
    with "Cannot resolve Kubernetes GVK" through new_object() and
    inflate(), contradicting the module's own documentation. The short
    names Sandbox, SandboxClaim, SandboxTemplate and SandboxWarmPool are
    unchanged and still resolve to the v1beta1 storage version.

  - AutoGen refuses a $ref it cannot resolve instead of dropping the
    property (k56). A property referencing a definition missing from
    the spec was never turned into an attribute; Moo ignores unknown
    constructor arguments, so inflation accepted the data and TO_JSON
    never emitted it again -- silent data loss on the round-trip.
    Behaviour change: a partial spec that references definitions it does
    not ship used to generate the class successfully, minus those fields,
    and now dies at class-generation time naming class and field. An
    opaque fallback was rejected because the DSL has no array-of-hash
    form, so items: { $ref: <missing> } would have become ArrayRef[Str]
    and rejected the very hashrefs the field carries -- k57's bug,
    reintroduced by the fix for this one. Still works: a top-level CRD
    schema whose metadata references the stock ObjectMeta without
    shipping its definition, because metadata is skipped first.

  - AutoGen handles additionalProperties given as a JSON boolean
    (k55). The boolean schema form is common in CRDs and killed class
    generation with "Not a HASH reference" and no class or field context.
    Both polarities now yield the same opaque hash a schemaless object
    gets; additionalProperties: false deliberately narrows nothing. An
    additionalProperties that is neither a schema object nor a boolean is
    a malformed schema and croaks naming class and field.

  - AutoGen maps boolean array items to an array of Bool (k57).
    items: { type: boolean } fell into the string default, so
    schema-conforming JSON booleans were rejected with a type error that
    never named the real problem. The generated attribute now reaches the
    DSL's per-element normalization. Internally the item types are
    Type::Tiny objects rather than barewords, because inside an arrayref
    the DSL reads a plain string as a class name for everything except
    'Str' and 'Int' -- ['Bool'] would have asked for an array of
    IO::K8s::Api::Bool objects.

  - AutoGen no longer generates apiVersion and kind as data attributes on
    classes that get GVK class methods (k60). $obj->kind("Other")
    was a silent no-op, and worse, apiVersion had no accessor collision
    at all: it stayed writable and its value overwrote the role-supplied
    one, so $obj->apiVersion("other/v9") produced a manifest claiming a
    GVK the class does not have. Same line k45 drew for the
    hand-written template classes. Classes without a GVK keep kind as an
    ordinary writable attribute.

  - set_owner() no longer writes ownerReferences the API server rejects
    (k47). Behaviour changes: an owner without a uid (anything built
    locally rather than read back from the cluster) is refused with a
    message naming the owner, instead of silently writing uid: "";
    controller is now a parameter ($obj->set_owner($owner, controller =>
    0|1), default 1 as before) and a second controller reference is
    refused, since Kubernetes allows at most one; adding the same owner
    (same uid) twice is an idempotent no-op instead of a duplicate entry;
    a non-controller reference omits the controller field entirely.
    blockOwnerDeletion stays unset (upstream defaults it to false).

  - A Bool attribute set explicitly to undef now stays unset instead of
    becoming false (k48). SecurityContext->new(privileged => undef)
    used to serialize as {"privileged":false} -- an explicit claim on the
    wire that overrides cluster- or admission-controller-set values under
    strategic-merge patch and server-side apply; now the field is simply
    omitted, matching what the inflation path always did. \undef likewise
    yields undef ("no value stays no value"). Behaviour change for callers
    who passed undef and relied on reading 0 back from the accessor. For
    the seven required Bool attributes (e.g. ContainerStatus ready) an
    explicit undef now means the field is missing at the API server instead
    of being sent as an invented false.

  - Bad data on a Bool field now dies with a diagnostic message instead of
    "Not a SCALAR reference at ... Resource.pm line NNN" (k42). A
    hashref/arrayref/coderef where a boolean was expected reports the
    reference type; the inflation path names the class and JSON field
    ("... while inflating IO::K8s::Api::Core::V1::PodSpec field
    hostNetwork"), the constructor path keeps Moo's attribute-naming
    wrapper, and a bad array element reports its index. Also fixed: a
    ref-to-a-ref (\\0) was silently true -- the exact bug k37 fixed,
    one dereference deeper; it now dies too. Blessed scalar refs
    (JSON::PP::Boolean and friends) keep working unchanged.

  - Internal: the apiextensions union classes (JSONSchemaPropsOrArray,
    JSONSchemaPropsOrBool, JSONSchemaPropsOrStringArray) now call
    _struct_to_object_expanded() for their hard-coded, fully-qualified
    JSONSchemaProps class name instead of the public struct_to_object()
    (k43), per the rule established in k35: callers that already
    hold a resolved class name skip re-expansion. No behaviour change.

  - Documentation: resource_plural's POD no longer promises a working REST
    path for every Kind (k44). For the fifteen Kinds on API tracks
    upstream no longer serves (e.g. Api::Resource::V1alpha3::DeviceClass),
    the group-fallback plural is correct for RBAC resources: rules -- and no
    other value would be better -- but the REST path built from it and the
    class's own api_version 404s against a current cluster because the track
    itself is dead. POD only, no behaviour change.

  - IO::K8s::List can now inflate a List-shaped payload (k46), matching
    what the README already claimed: `$k8s->json_to_object($podlist_json)`
    and `struct_to_object()` route any `kind` ending in `List` (or the bare
    `kind: List`) to a new `IO::K8s::List->FROM_STRUCT`, which derives the
    item type from the list's own Kind-minus-'List' and apiVersion (a real
    API list response carries neither on its items) and inflates each item
    fully. `item_class` remains available, now also as a sibling key in the
    struct, to override the derived type for a generic `kind: List` payload
    that has nothing to derive from. An item Kind that cannot be resolved
    dies with the same "Cannot resolve Kubernetes GVK" error every other
    entry point uses -- never a silently empty or half-inflated list.
    Previously this died with "Cannot resolve Kubernetes GVK: kind
    'PodList', ..." (no *List classes have existed since 1.105) or, via a
    direct `struct_to_object('+IO::K8s::List', ...)` call, with an unrelated
    "Can't locate object method _k8s_attr_info" error.

  - IO::K8s::List::item_class now only accepts a fully-qualified class name
    (k49), matching the '+' convention used everywhere else in this
    distribution: a leading `+` is stripped before the class is loaded, and
    a short or partially-qualified name (e.g. `'Pod'` instead of
    `'IO::K8s::Api::Core::V1::Pod'`) is not guessed at. Behaviour change:
    `kind()` now returns `undef` for such a name instead of a guessed Kind
    string (`'PodList'`) that `api_version()` could never confirm --
    IO::K8s::List never serializes a `kind` without an `apiVersion`
    alongside it, in either direction now.

  - Stop stamping apiVersion/kind into seven embedded template classes that
    the upstream schema carries no such keys for (k45): PodTemplateSpec,
    JobTemplateSpec, PersistentVolumeClaimTemplate, and ResourceClaimTemplateSpec
    (v1, v1alpha3, v1beta1, v1beta2). Each composed IO::K8s::APIObject, so
    TO_JSON emitted the pair on every embedded occurrence -- most visibly
    spec.template on every Deployment, StatefulSet, DaemonSet, ReplicaSet,
    Job and CronJob this distribution serializes. The upstream OpenAPI
    definitions for these seven declare only metadata and spec, with no
    x-kubernetes-group-version-kind, and kubectl's default strict field
    validation rejects unrecognized fields rather than pruning them, so the
    extra pair was liable to make `kubectl apply` reject otherwise-valid
    output (not verified against a live cluster; this describes the
    validation behaviour, not an observed failure). Contrast case, left
    unchanged: Core::V1::PersistentVolumeClaim (embedded in
    StatefulSetSpec.volumeClaimTemplates) genuinely carries inline TypeMeta
    upstream and keeps emitting apiVersion/kind.
    Breaking change: all seven now compose IO::K8s::Resource instead of
    IO::K8s::APIObject, with an explicit C<k8s metadata> declaration in
    place of the role-derived one. C<metadata> is unaffected, but
    C<api_version()>, C<kind()>, C<add_label()>, C<add_annotation()> and the
    other IO::K8s::Role::APIObject convenience methods are no longer public
    methods on instances of these seven classes -- calling one now fails
    with "Can't locate object method" instead of returning a value.

  - Derive IO::K8s::List::kind() for a single-segment item_class too
    (k41). The same missing '::' as the previous entry, in the
    item_class fallback -- which is precisely the empty-list case, where
    there is no first item to ask. An empty list of a single-segment Kind
    therefore serialized apiVersion without kind:. The non-empty path was
    already fixed by k38, since it asks the item.

  - Derive kind() for a single-segment class from the whole class name
    (k38). A CRD registered as a top-level package -- reached as
    '+Widget' or through a resource_map value of '+Widget' -- has no '::',
    so kind() returned undef and TO_JSON emitted a manifest with no kind:
    at all, which the API server rejects. k35 had just made those
    names reliably reachable, so the class was usable and its output was
    not. set_owner() was worse than silent there: OwnerReference declares
    kind as a required Str, so an undef kind made it die outright.
    api_version() and resource_plural() are unaffected -- both key off an
    IO::K8s:: prefix, so the '::' is guaranteed by the time they parse.

  - Document the fail-closed guarantee of the GVK entry points (k40).
    new_object, inflate, json_to_object and struct_to_object all die on an
    unresolvable GVK request rather than substituting a different version or
    a similarly-named class, and a bare unqualified name is deliberately
    exempt -- behaviour that was tested but stated nowhere. POD only.

  - Fail closed on an unresolvable GVK in every entry point, not just
    new_object (k39). A name carrying its apiVersion inside the string,
    'nonexistent.io/v1/UnknownKind', is an exact GVK request and comes back
    from expand_class as undef. Only new_object turned that into the
    intended "Cannot resolve Kubernetes GVK: kind ..., apiVersion ...";
    json_to_object, struct_to_object and inflate passed the undef on to
    load_class and died out of Module::Runtime with "argument is not a
    module name", which names neither the kind nor the apiVersion. inflate
    had the guard on its explicit-apiVersion branch only, so the
    single-argument forms and load_yaml, which all route through it,
    inherited the hole. All four now share one check. A name without a
    domain qualifier is deliberately not affected: expand_class still falls
    back to IO::K8s::<Name> there, so an unknown bare Kind keeps failing on
    the missing module rather than on GVK resolution.

  - Stop boolean fields reading an unblessed \0 as true (k37). The
    is_bool branch of struct_to_object/inflate tested the reference itself,
    and every reference is true in Perl, so the classic Perl false idiom
    arrived as true -- and came back out blessed as a JSON::PP::Boolean,
    indistinguishable downstream from a correct one. On a field like
    privileged, allowPrivilegeEscalation or hostNetwork that is a silent
    flip in the unsafe direction. Blessed JSON booleans and plain 0/1 were
    never affected, nor was load_yaml, whose default yields plain 0/1.

  - Stop boolean fields reading the string "false" as true (k37, found
    while fixing the above). A non-empty string is truthy in Perl, so
    "false" and "False" became 1 -- the same silent flip, and on both paths:
    the inflation path and the constructor, where SecurityContext->new(
    privileged => "false") returned 1. Behaviour change for callers who
    passed the string and relied on the old answer. Both paths now share one
    normalization in IO::K8s::Resource, which is what let the two disagree
    in the first place. One narrow case changes from wrong-but-quiet to
    loud: a hashref or arrayref on a boolean field used to be taken as true
    and now dies, which is the same class of bad data this pair of entries
    is about.

  - Read a bare one-word class name as a Kubernetes Kind, never as a
    package name (k35). k34 put the resource_map ahead of
    expand_class's "is there a loadable class of exactly this name?" probe,
    which made every registered Kind safe but left a window for Kinds the
    model does not know: with an openapi_spec defining kind "Widget" and an
    unrelated top-level Widget.pm installed, expand_class('Widget') returned
    the foreign distribution instead of the generated class. Single-segment
    names now skip that probe entirely and continue to IO::K8s::<Kind> and
    then to auto-generation; multi-segment names ('My::StaticWebSite') keep
    it, which is the documented CRD case. To name a single-segment class of
    your own, prefix it -- '+Widget' -- or use class_namespaces or a
    resource_map entry. The failure mode changes for one narrow case: a
    consumer who relied on a bare 'Widget' resolving to an installed
    top-level Widget now gets IO::K8s::Widget, which fails to load.

  - Stop struct_to_object re-expanding a class name its caller had already
    resolved (k35). new_object(), json_to_object() and the nested-object
    inflation all called expand_class() and then handed the result to
    struct_to_object(), which ran the full search order over it a second
    time -- so an exactly-resolved name could be re-interpreted. Concretely,
    new_object('+Secret', \%args) resolved to 'Secret' and the second pass
    found 'Secret' in the resource_map, returning
    IO::K8s::Api::Core::V1::Secret instead of the caller's class: the '+'
    prefix's guarantee of an exact class was lost on every new_object and
    json_to_object. These callers now use a pre-expanded internal path.
    struct_to_object() itself is unchanged for consumers and still expands
    the short names it is given.

  - Resolve resource_plural for Kinds on API tracks upstream no longer
    serves (k36). The generated table from the previous entry is keyed
    by exact GVK, so the 15 shipped classes on dropped tracks
    (resource.k8s.io/v1alpha3, flowcontrol/v1beta3,
    storage.k8s.io/v1alpha1 and others) still had no plural. A second
    generated tier keyed "group|Kind" now answers those, consulted only
    after the exact-GVK lookup misses. This is upstream data, not a
    heuristic: RBAC addresses resources by apiGroups plus resources with no
    version at all, so the plural is a property of the GroupResource, and
    the generator emits a group-level entry only where every version in the
    spec agrees on it -- dying otherwise rather than picking one. Kinds
    carrying a plural rose from 95 to 110 of the 120 shipped API classes.
    Still no bare-Kind fallback and still no guessing: core/v1 Event and
    events.k8s.io/v1 Event remain distinct, and the subresources plus the
    embedded *TemplateSpec types keep returning undef.

  - Give the shipped Kinds a real resource_plural (k33).
    IO::K8s::Role::APIObject::resource_plural returned undef for every
    built-in class, so consumers needing Kind -> plural -- RBAC speaks
    plurals, the API speaks Kinds -- had to fall back to an lc+s guess,
    where a wrong plural is indistinguishable from a denied permission.
    The role now carries a table keyed "$api_version/Kind", so
    core/v1 Event and events.k8s.io/v1 Event stay distinct, and
    class_namespaces subclasses inherit through @ISA exactly as they do
    for api_version. The values are generated from the collection REST
    paths of the upstream OpenAPI spec, not derived -- Endpoints is
    endpoints, NetworkPolicy is networkpolicies, Ingress is ingresses --
    and maint/spec-resource-plural-gen.pl regenerates the block at the
    next upstream sync. An explicit resource_plural on a CRD or from
    IO::K8s::AutoGen still wins. There is deliberately no heuristic
    fallback: Kinds with no collection endpoint of their own, such as the
    Eviction, Scale and TokenRequest subresources, keep returning undef.

  - Stop bare Kind short names from resolving to an identically-named
    installed CPAN module (GH #7, GH #8). expand_class() probed for a
    loaded-or-loadable class of exactly the given name before consulting
    the resource_map, and that probe loads rather than merely tests -- so on
    a machine that happened to have the CPAN distributions Event or Role
    installed, expand_class('Event') returned Event instead of
    IO::K8s::Api::Core::V1::Event and the caller then died in
    _k8s_attr_info. The probe now runs after the resource_map and after
    class_namespaces, so a registered Kind always wins over a same-named
    package; '+Full::Class' still forces an exact class, and a CRD class
    named in full is still loaded on demand. All 78 short names in the
    default resource_map were exposed; reported from CPAN smokers.

  - IO::K8s::AutoGen reuses a shipped core class for a nested schema of
    exactly its shape (D5) instead of generating a new one: a CRD's inline
    LabelSelector, HTTPHeader-shaped struct, and the like are now typed as
    the real IO::K8s class rather than a per-provider copy. On by default;
    IO::K8s::CRD->generate and IO::K8s->add_crd (as a trailing options
    hashref, e.g. add_crd($path, { reuse_core => 0 })) turn it off. A
    shape under two keys is never reused, and every candidate must be
    type-compatible with the schema key by key; several surviving
    candidates are resolved to the preferred one (LabelSelector family,
    then the rest of Meta::V1, then core/v1, then alphabetically) only
    when they are wire-identical (same type per key, ignoring
    required-ness, and the same referenced class per key) -- {name,value}
    reuses HTTPHeader over PodDNSConfigOption/Sysctl, {key,operator,values}
    reuses LabelSelectorRequirement over FieldSelectorRequirement/
    NodeSelectorRequirement even though it spans two API areas. A shape
    shared by candidates that are NOT wire-identical, such as
    {metadata,spec} (PodTemplateSpec, JobTemplateSpec,
    ResourceClaimTemplateSpec and others each type spec differently),
    stays a nested class rather than guess. New
    IO::K8s::AutoGen::core_class_for_shape(\@json_keys) lists shipped
    classes matching a given key set (name only, preference-ordered) --
    metadata counts as part of the shape for an embedded type but not for
    a top-level Kind.

  - The bundled CRD providers (Cilium, Traefik, CertManager, GatewayAPI,
    K3s, AgentSandbox, and the reserved PrometheusOperator, VolumeSnapshot,
    ExternalSecrets) join IO::K8s::Resource's class-prefix map, so a
    provider class is written the short way a core class is
    ('Traefik::V1alpha1::MiddlewareSpec' like 'Core::V1::PodSpec') instead
    of always spelling out '+IO::K8s::Traefik::V1alpha1::MiddlewareSpec';
    the new IO::K8s::Resource::class_prefixes() exposes the map read-only.
    IO::K8s::CRD::Emitter renders those short references (longest matching
    namespace first) and gains an overlay attribute -- the per-Kind slice
    of a provider's forthcoming maint/crd-render/<Provider>.yaml -- that
    supplies the root class's with roles (one with line, defaulting to
    Namespaced when the Kind is one and to no roles otherwise), verbatim
    extra source lines right after it, and a names map from a nested
    class's logical path (IO::K8s::AutoGen::class_path) to its bare
    (upstream Go) package name, checked after the existing class-name-keyed
    names map.

  - Traefik modeled to full depth (D5, k95): all 10 traefik.io/v1alpha1
    Kinds' spec fields are now typed object graphs -- 86 classes total (10
    Kinds + 76 nested), named after the upstream traefik/traefik v3.7.12
    Go types, checked in under IO::K8s::Traefik::V1alpha1::*. A shared Go
    type used by several Kinds (Service, ServerHealthCheck, Sticky,
    Cookie, IPStrategy, ProxyProtocol, RootCA, Spiffe, Domain,
    Certificate, ...) is one class, not a copy per Kind; a middleware
    reference, TLS option/store reference and similar {name, namespace}
    shapes reuse Core::V1::SecretReference (reuse_core) instead of a
    provider-local class. None of the 10 Kinds declares a status
    subresource upstream, so IngressRoute/Middleware/.../TraefikService no
    longer have a status field at all -- constructing with status => {...}
    now keeps the value in the unknown-fields bag (re-emitted on the wire)
    rather than a real attribute, same as any other undeclared key.
    Constructing spec (or any of its nested fields) via a raw
    ->new(spec => { ... }) no longer coerces the hashref (k100, pre-
    existing); build via new_object/inflate, or seed a typed spec through
    spec_set/spec_push/spec_merge, which do coerce.

1.107     2026-08-15 15:37:52Z

  - Resolve resource_map short-name keys on the explicit-apiVersion path
    (k31). expand_class('Kind', $api_version) and the qualified-string
    form now fall back to the resource_map's bare short-name key when no
    '$api_version/Kind' key exists, but only if the mapped class itself
    confirms the requested version via api_version() — a CRD registered as
    'StaticWebSite => "+My::StaticWebSite"' inflates again from a manifest
    hashref instead of dying with "Cannot resolve Kubernetes GVK". The
    fail-closed semantics from k17 are preserved: a class that cannot
    verify the requested version is never substituted — whether it reports
    a different version, has no api_version() method, returns undef from it,
    or implements api_version as an instance attribute so that the class
    method call dies. The fallback runs before openapi_spec AutoGen, since
    the user explicitly registered the class.

  - Stop add() from dying on a provider class whose api_version is an
    instance attribute (k32). Merging a resource_map — via
    IO::K8s->new(with => [...]) or ->add(...) — asks each mapped class for
    its api_version() to build the domain-qualified key. A class that
    implements api_version as a Moo attribute rather than a constant made
    that class-method call die, taking the whole merge with it. Such a
    class is now registered under its short name and simply skipped for
    the qualified key, which is the only correct answer: no qualified key
    can be derived for it.

1.106     2026-08-13 02:59:43Z

  - Derive api_version through @ISA for class_namespaces subclasses.
    IO::K8s::Role::APIObject::api_version now falls back to walking the
    inheritance chain when the class name itself is not in a known
    namespace, so a consumer subclass (e.g. `use parent
    'IO::K8s::Api::Core::V1::Pod'`) serializes apiVersion instead of
    silently omitting it.

  - Make compare_to_schema inheritance-aware. The schema comparison in
    IO::K8s::Role::Resource now reads the merged @ISA attribute view
    (_k8s_attr_info) instead of the raw registry entry, so a
    class_namespaces-style subclass compares its inherited attributes
    instead of an empty or partial set.

  - Make the k8s attribute lookups class_namespaces-aware via @ISA.
    _k8s_attr_info and _k8s_attributes in IO::K8s::Role::Resource now walk
    the inheritance chain, so a consumer subclass registered through
    class_namespaces (e.g. `use parent 'IO::K8s::Api::Core::V1::Pod'`)
    inflates with typed fields and serializes its parents' attributes
    instead of seeing an empty registry. Attribute info merges nearest-wins
    (a class's own declaration overrides an inherited one, in deterministic
    @ISA order); the attribute list is a deduplicated union of own and
    inherited declarations. Both merged views are cached per class and
    invalidated when a new k8s attribute is registered.

  - Made AutoGen dispatch apiVersion-aware and deterministic.
    expand_class()/inflate() with an explicit apiVersion now fall through to
    the openapi_spec AutoGen lookup when the resource map has no qualified
    key, but only for an exact group/version match in the spec's
    x-kubernetes-group-version-kind metadata; unknown or non-matching
    apiVersions fail closed (expand_class returns undef, inflate dies)
    instead of silently selecting a different version. Definition lookup no
    longer depends on hash order: versionless lookups sort candidate
    definitions lexicographically, exact lookups filter by group/version
    and croak on ambiguity. AutoGen picks a multi-GVK definition's entry by
    exact api_version (croak on ambiguity or no match) and deterministically
    sorted first otherwise, and a definition serving several versions now
    gets a GVK-specific package identity so two apiVersions of one
    definition yield distinct classes with the correct api_version method
    and wire serialization.

  - Fix IO::K8s::List::api_version for empty lists with an item_class.
    The local class-name regex derived shortened, invalid wire versions
    for groups with a ".k8s.io" suffix (rbac/v1, storage/v1, events/v1)
    and serialised them into manifests. The wire version is now derived
    from the item_class's own api_version class method, which knows the
    full group (rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1, storage.k8s.io/v1,
    events.k8s.io/v1); unloadable or non-API item_classes yield undef and
    serialised empty lists omit apiVersion again.

  - Document that .pk8s manifests are Perl code executed in-process via
    eval and therefore must only be loaded from trusted sources, with
    load_yaml documented as the data-only path without code execution.

  - Declared Module::Runtime as a direct runtime prerequisite. IO::K8s has
    always loaded it in IO::K8s (for require_module) but cpanfile and the
    built META omitted it, so dependency installers that resolve strictly
    from the declared prereqs could miss it. The built META.json now lists
    Module::Runtime under runtime requires.

  - Made built-in Kubernetes resource dispatch exact for every addressable
    apiVersion/kind pair in the pinned v1.36.3 OpenAPI spec. This adds the
    missing events.k8s.io/v1 Event and autoscaling/v1
    HorizontalPodAutoscaler routes while preserving the historical bare-name
    defaults (Core v1 Event and Autoscaling v2 HPA). Explicit unknown,
    malformed, empty, or mismatched apiVersions now fail closed:
    expand_class() returns undef and inflate()/new_object() report the
    requested Kind and apiVersion instead of silently selecting a different
    bare-name schema. Newly exposed compatibility aliases are
    ClusterTrustBundle, DeviceTaintRule, LeaseCandidate, PodGroup,
    ResourcePoolStatusRequest, StorageVersion, StorageVersionMigration and
    Workload; all existing aliases and targets remain pinned. An offline,
    SHA-256-pinned v1.36.3 fixture now exhaustively checks 98 addressable GVKs,
    all 14 multi-version Kind collisions, namespace scope, maintained
    non-dispatchable exceptions, real inflation and provider first-wins
    behavior.

  - Fixed inflate()/expand_class() to dispatch by apiVersion to the correct
    multi-version Kind. Pre-fix, %DEFAULT_RESOURCE_MAP mapped each short
    Kind name (DeviceClass, ResourceClaim, ResourceClaimTemplate,
    ResourceSlice, ...) to exactly one class path (always the GA v1), and
    only entries added externally via add() ever got domain-qualified
    ('$apiVersion/$Kind') entries. Two visible consequences:
    inflate({apiVersion=>'resource.k8s.io/v1beta1', kind=>'DeviceClass',
    ...}) silently returned IO::K8s::Api::Resource::V1::DeviceClass (the
    GA class, wrong schema), and inflate of a short-name-less Kind
    (DeviceTaintRule, ResourcePoolStatusRequest) died with 'Cant locate
    IO/K8s/DeviceTaintRule.pm in @INC' because the bare IO::K8s::$Kind
    fallback does not exist. %DEFAULT_RESOURCE_MAP now carries literal
    qualified entries for every shipped version of every addressable Kind,
    including the short-name-less ones. Class-method and instance dispatch
    therefore share the same complete static map without BUILD eagerly
    loading every target class; add() still derives qualified keys for
    externally merged providers. See k11.
  - Fixed api_version() in IO::K8s::Role::APIObject for the
    Storagemigration and Apiserverinternal groups. The fallback
    `lc($group) . '/' . $version` only produces the correct wire
    apiVersion for groups whose CamelCase lc-form equals the upstream
    group name (apps, batch, autoscaling, policy) -- for groups whose
    upstream name has a `.k8s.io` suffix, it produced a syntactically
    plausible but rejected-by-the-API-server string. In particular,
    every serialised StorageVersionMigration manifested as
    `apiVersion: storagemigration/v1beta1` (upstream:
    `storagemigration.k8s.io/v1beta1`) and every StorageVersion as
    `apiVersion: apiserverinternal/v1alpha1` (upstream:
    `internal.apiserver.k8s.io/v1alpha1`). Both groups are now in
    %API_GROUP_MAP, alongside the 13 already-mapped groups. The other
    18 groups covered by %_class_prefix were audited and verified to
    either already map correctly or to fall through to the lc-fallback
    correctly (the upstream group name equals the lc form).
  - Fixed _expand_class in IO::K8s::Resource to handle CamelCase prefixes
    (KubeAggregator, AdmissionRegistration, ...). The single-word
    `[A-Z][a-z]+` regex could not match a prefix that has an internal
    capital, so any declared class name whose first segment was CamelCase
    silently fell through to the IO::K8s::Api default. In practice this
    meant KubeAggregator's APIService, APIServiceSpec, APIServiceStatus,
    APIServiceCondition and ServiceReference could not be inflated --
    spec/status resolved to nonexistent IO::K8s::Api::KubeAggregator::V1
    classes instead of the shipped IO::K8s::KubeAggregator::Pkg::Apis::
    Apiregistration::V1 ones. The lookup now walks %_class_prefix in
    longest-key-first order so CamelCase wins over a hypothetical shorter
    substring, and uses \Q ... \E so the prefix is matched as a literal
    rather than as a regex. Backwards-compatible: unknown short names still
    fall through to the IO::K8s::Api default.
  - Shipped IO::K8s::Api::Apiserverinternal::V1alpha1::StorageVersionSpec.
    Upstream declares it as an empty struct ("StorageVersionSpec is an
    empty spec"), but the class was never authored, so every StorageVersion
    inflate died with "Can't locate .../StorageVersionSpec.pm in @INC".
    There was no working path through the class. This is the empty class
    upstream asked for; the failure mode that mattered was on the
    serialisation side, where an empty class round-tripped through TO_JSON
    could collapse to an empty hash or disappear altogether.
  - Added t/34_registry_guard.t: after every shipped class is loaded,
    walks the global attribute registry and asserts every referenced
    target class is loadable. This is the regression net that would have
    caught the apiextensions.k8s.io/v1 union types, the KubeAggregator
    prefix mismatch and the missing StorageVersionSpec together, rather
    than one at a time on the consumer side. Inline-generated structs
    (packages with no .pm file) are recognised via the `k8s` symbol in
    the target's stash.
  - Added t/32_kubeaggregator_apiservice.t and t/33_apiserverinternal_
    storage_version.t covering the two regression cases above: that
    APIService and StorageVersion inflate, that every spec/status/
    condition class resolves to the namespace shipped (not the wrong
    IO::K8s::Api fallback), and that the full object round-trips
    byte-for-byte through inflate -> TO_JSON -> inflate -> TO_JSON.
  - Added t/35_expand_class.t and t/36_storage_version_spec_unit.t for
    direct unit coverage of the bugfix targets: every branch of
    Resource::_expand_class (+FullClassName, already-qualified,
    longest-key-first prefix walk, default fallback) and the full
    prefix map; and StorageVersionSpec on its own (DOES Resource,
    ->new, TO_JSON as an empty hash, no api_version/kind since the
    class intentionally does not consume IO::K8s::APIObject).

  - Added the four apiextensions.k8s.io/v1 types the distribution declared
    but never shipped: JSON, JSONSchemaPropsOrArray, JSONSchemaPropsOrBool
    and JSONSchemaPropsOrStringArray. Without them, inflating any
    CustomResourceDefinition whose schema used `items`, `additionalItems`,
    `additionalProperties`, `dependencies`, `default`, `example` or `enum`
    died with "Can't locate IO/K8s/.../JSONSchemaPropsOrArray.pm in @INC" --
    in practice nearly every real CRD, since a single array field is enough
    to hit it. All four are Kubernetes union types that serialize as the
    bare alternative rather than as a tagged wrapper, so which arm was used
    now survives a round trip: `additionalProperties: false` stays false
    instead of collapsing into an empty schema object, and a single `items`
    schema does not turn into a one-element array.
  - Added a FROM_STRUCT inflation hook to struct_to_object. A class that
    provides this class method takes over its own inflation completely and
    owns its TO_JSON in return, instead of being built field by field from
    a hashref. This is what makes the union types above representable; it
    is the general mechanism for any type that serializes as a bare value.

  - Shipped resource.k8s.io/v1beta1 (39 classes, entirely missing --
    lib/IO/K8s/Api/Resource/ had no V1beta1/ directory at all) and filled
    in resource.k8s.io/v1beta2 (39 more classes; only the DeviceTaintRule/
    DeviceTaintRuleSpec/DeviceTaintRuleStatus/DeviceTaintSelector quartet
    from an earlier fix was shipped there). Both versions now carry the
    full DRA surface: DeviceClass, ResourceClaim, ResourceClaimTemplate and
    ResourceSlice (DeviceClass/ResourceSlice cluster scoped, ResourceClaim/
    ResourceClaimTemplate namespaced -- verified against the real swagger
    paths, not just pattern-matched from V1) plus the whole Device/
    AllocationResult/DeviceRequest/Counter/CapacityRequestPolicy family.
    v1beta1 is the most widely deployed DRA server version; any consumer
    talking to a cluster that had not migrated to v1 got "Can't locate
    .../DeviceClass.pm in @INC" for every one of these Kinds.
  - Added the 9 v1.36 DRA additions to resource.k8s.io/v1alpha3 that had
    not been backported to the legacy "classic DRA" version also serving
    them: DeviceTaint, DeviceTaintRule (+ Spec/Status), DeviceTaintSelector,
    PoolStatus, and ResourcePoolStatusRequest (+ Spec/Status) -- the latter
    three were already present from a previous pass; only the
    DeviceTaint(Rule) family was actually missing. The 24 already-shipped
    "classic DRA" structural types (DeviceClass, ResourceClaim, Device,
    AllocationResult, etc.) are untouched, per the 1.100/1.105 decision to
    keep them as legacy backward compatibility.
  - Fixed ArrayRef[Bool] fields (DeviceAttribute.bools, present in the V1,
    V1beta1 and V1beta2 DRA APIs) to serialize as JSON booleans instead of
    plain 0/1, and to accept real decoded JSON booleans on the way back in.
    Previously TO_JSON emitted [1,0,1] instead of [true,false,true], and
    FROM_HASH on a real cluster response died with a Moo type constraint
    violation because JSON::PP::Boolean objects don't satisfy Types::
    Standard's Bool -- this affected the already-shipped
    IO::K8s::Api::Resource::V1::DeviceAttribute too, not just the new
    v1beta1/v1beta2 copies. IO::K8s::Resource now tracks an
    is_array_of_bool flag with element-wise coercion, mirroring the
    existing scalar Bool handling.
  - Fixed ResourceClaimTemplateSpec (v1beta1 and v1beta2) to be built on
    IO::K8s::APIObject instead of IO::K8s::Resource, matching the already-
    shipped V1 sibling. Despite not being a Kind, it carries a real
    upstream `metadata: ObjectMeta` field; without APIObject the metadata
    attribute was never registered and silently dropped on serialization.
  - Added maint/spec-drift-check.pl, a repeatable coverage checker that
    diffs a real upstream swagger.json against what lib/IO/K8s/ actually
    ships and reports missing Kinds/types/fields (the tool behind
    k4-k8's discovery), plus a --from/--to mode that diffs two upstream
    releases directly to gauge whether a version bump is worth doing.
    Settled non-gaps (dropped *List kinds, old back-compat API tracks,
    apimachinery scalar/opaque types) are filtered via the maintained
    maint/spec-drift-exceptions.yaml. Report-only: never edits lib/ or
    the karr board.
  - Shipped storagemigration.k8s.io/v1beta1 (IO::K8s::Api::Storagemigration::
    V1beta1::StorageVersionMigration, ::StorageVersionMigrationSpec and
    ::StorageVersionMigrationStatus), the version v1.36 clusters actually
    serve now that v1alpha1 has been dropped from the upstream spec. The
    existing V1alpha1 classes are untouched and stay shipped for old-cluster
    back-compat. Also added IO::K8s::Apimachinery::Pkg::Apis::Meta::V1::
    GroupResource, which StorageVersionMigrationSpec.resource needs and
    which did not exist under any group.
  - Added five Core::V1 classes that existing structs gained a new $ref
    field for in v1.36, but whose target type was never shipped, silently
    swallowing the field on inflate: FileKeySelector (EnvVarSource.
    fileKeyRef -- read an env var's value from a file in the container),
    NodeSwapStatus (NodeSystemInfo.swap), PodCertificateProjection
    (VolumeProjection.podCertificate), and VolumeStatus + ImageVolumeStatus
    (VolumeMountStatus.volumeStatus).
  - Added t/38_storagemigration_v1beta1_and_core_v136_fields.t covering the
    two fixes above: a full StorageVersionMigration inflate -> TO_JSON ->
    inflate round-trip through GroupResource, plus round-trips for
    EnvVarSource.fileKeyRef, VolumeMountStatus.volumeStatus, NodeSystemInfo.
    swap and VolumeProjection.podCertificate.
  - Added 14 fields the v1.36 sync had missed on otherwise-shipped classes:
    Core::V1::ContainerStatus.stopSignal, Core::V1::Lifecycle.stopSignal,
    Core::V1::PodCondition.observedGeneration, Core::V1::
    PodSecurityContext.seLinuxChangePolicy, Core::V1::ResourceHealth.message,
    Storage::V1::VolumeError.errorCode, ApiextensionsApiserver::...::V1::
    CustomResourceDefinitionCondition.observedGeneration and ::
    CustomResourceDefinitionStatus.observedGeneration, Apimachinery::...::
    Meta::V1::DeleteOptions.ignoreStoreReadErrorWithClusterBreakingPotential,
    and Apimachinery::Pkg::Version::Info.emulationMajor/emulationMinor/
    minCompatibilityMajor/minCompatibilityMinor. Also shipped the new
    IO::K8s::Apimachinery::Pkg::Apis::Meta::V1::ShardInfo struct and wired it
    up as ListMeta.shardInfo, which previously had no target type at all.
  - Shipped coordination.k8s.io/v1alpha2 (IO::K8s::Api::Coordination::
    V1alpha2::LeaseCandidate and ::LeaseCandidateSpec), which had no
    directory at all despite V1, V1alpha1 and V1beta1 all being shipped.
    Also added IO::K8s::Api::Scheduling::V1alpha2::TypedLocalObjectReference,
    a distinct upstream schema that WorkloadSpec.controllerRef previously
    pointed at Core::V1::TypedLocalObjectReference for instead -- the two
    happen to share the same three fields today, but they are different
    schemas and were drifting apart silently.
  - Added the meta.v1 discovery Kinds APIGroupList and APIResourceList
    (IO::K8s::Apimachinery::Pkg::Apis::Meta::V1::), used by the /apis and
    /apis/<group> discovery endpoints. Modelled like their already-shipped
    siblings APIGroup/APIVersions/Status/DeleteOptions: explicit apiVersion/
    kind Str fields, not IO::K8s::APIObject.
  - Added t/39_v1_36_field_and_kind_gaps.t covering all of the above: field
    round-trips for a representative sample of the 14 additions, a full
    LeaseCandidate inflate -> TO_JSON -> inflate round-trip, the corrected
    WorkloadSpec.controllerRef target class, and APIGroupList/
    APIResourceList loading with their required fields passed through.

1.105     2026-08-08 18:51:44Z

  - Removed the 76 individual *List classes (PodList, ServiceList,
    DeploymentList, etc.) that have emitted "use IO::K8s::List instead"
    deprecation warnings since the 1.00 Moose-to-Moo rewrite. They were
    never real classes in the 1.x series and this release drops them from
    the distribution entirely. Code that still references one of these
    names (e.g. via cpanfile or `use`) will now fail to install instead of
    silently warning; install IO::K8s::Deprecated for a clear redirect
    message pointing at IO::K8s::List. This also removes four namespaces
    that held nothing but a List stub and are now gone entirely --
    IO::K8s::ApiExtensionsApiServer, IO::K8s::Api::Auditregistration,
    IO::K8s::Api::Extensions, IO::K8s::Api::Settings -- plus several
    now-empty single-version subdirectories under Apps, Autoscaling, Batch,
    Certificates, Coordination, Events, KubeAggregator, Policy, Rbac, and
    Scheduling. Full old-name list: IO::K8s::Deprecated's POD.
  - Restored the 8 Cilium v2alpha1/v2 classes dropped in 1.100's Cilium
    v1.19.2 upgrade (CiliumBGPAdvertisement, CiliumBGPClusterConfig,
    CiliumBGPNodeConfig, CiliumBGPNodeConfigOverride, CiliumBGPPeerConfig,
    CiliumCIDRGroup under Cilium::V2alpha1; CiliumBGPPeeringPolicy under
    Cilium::V2alpha1; CiliumExternalWorkload under Cilium::V2). These now
    ship alongside their current-API-version siblings for backward
    compatibility with clusters still running older Cilium releases,
    matching this dist's existing convention of keeping multiple API
    versions of a resource side by side (e.g. Apps V1beta1/V1beta2/V1).
  - Synced all API surfaces to their current upstream releases (previous
    target: Kubernetes v1.31 and CRD providers pinned months/years back).
    Kubernetes core moved v1.31 -> v1.36; CRD providers moved
    Cilium v1.19.2 -> v1.20.0, K3s v1.35.1+k3s1 -> v1.36.3+k3s1,
    Traefik v3.0.0 -> v3.7.10 (CRD set unchanged across v3.x),
    cert-manager v1.19.3 -> v1.21.1 (no CRD/field changes),
    Gateway API v1.1.0 -> v1.6.1, Agent Sandbox v0.2.1 -> v0.5.4.
    * Cilium: added CiliumDatapathPlugin (cilium.io/v2alpha1, new in
      v1.20.0's Extensible Datapath feature).
    * Gateway API: added BackendTLSPolicy, ListenerSet, TLSRoute,
      TCPRoute, UDPRoute (all gateway.networking.k8s.io/v1), and a
      gateway.networking.k8s.io/v1 ReferenceGrant alongside the existing
      v1beta1 (still the short-name/storage version); TLSRoute joins
      HTTPRoute/GRPCRoute in consuming IO::K8s::Role::Routable.
    * Agent Sandbox: all four CRDs gained a v1beta1 track (now the
      storage version) with real schema changes -- Sandbox drops
      spec/status.replicas for spec.operatingMode + spec.service +
      status.nodeName/podIPs; SandboxClaim drops spec.sandboxTemplateRef
      for a required spec.warmPoolRef and gains
      spec.additionalPodMetadata, spec.env, spec.lifecycle,
      a typed spec.volumeClaimTemplates list, and
      status.sandbox.name (was status.sandbox.Name); SandboxTemplate
      gains spec.envVarsInjectionPolicy, spec.service,
      spec.volumeClaimTemplates, spec.volumeClaimTemplatesPolicy;
      SandboxWarmPool gains spec.updateStrategy.type. v1alpha1 survives
      as served-but-deprecated on all four.
    * K3s and cert-manager: version bump only, no CRD/field-level changes
      upstream.
    * Traefik: version bump only; CRD set confirmed unchanged across the
      whole v3.x line.
    * Core Kubernetes -- workloads: added container restart rules
      (Container/EphemeralContainer restartPolicyRules), pod-level
      resources (PodSpec.resources, PodStatus.allocatedResources/
      resources), PodSpec.hostnameOverride and .schedulingGroup (gang
      scheduling), PodStatus.observedGeneration and DRA-related extended
      resource claim status fields, HorizontalPodAutoscaler per-direction
      scaling tolerance, DeploymentStatus/ReplicaSetStatus
      .terminatingReplicas, NodeStatus.declaredFeatures.
    * Core Kubernetes -- networking: added networking.k8s.io/v1
      ServiceCIDR and IPAddress (stable since v1.33; deprecated v1beta1
      kept alongside), made NetworkPolicySpec.podSelector optional
      (upstream now defaults it), added discovery.k8s.io/v1 EndpointHints
      .forNodes / ForNode for PreferSameNode topology routing.
    * Core Kubernetes -- security/admission: added
      MutatingAdmissionPolicy/MutatingAdmissionPolicyBinding (GA in v1),
      PodCertificateRequest (certificates.k8s.io/v1beta1), and
      ClusterTrustBundle at v1beta1 alongside the existing v1alpha1.
      The older v1alpha1/v1beta1 ValidatingAdmissionPolicy and
      authentication.k8s.io/{v1alpha1,v1beta1} SelfSubjectReview tracks,
      and flowcontrol.apiserver.k8s.io/v1beta3, were evaluated for
      removal (no longer served by a v1.36 apiserver) but kept in this
      release rather than deleted, matching this dist's Cilium-precedent
      of preferring backward compatibility over deletion for classes that
      already shipped in a prior CPAN release -- deleting a
      previously-released module name without a tombstone would orphan
      it on PAUSE. Left as a maintainer decision for a future release.
    * Core Kubernetes -- storage/DRA: added resource.k8s.io/v1 (GA)
      Dynamic Resource Allocation -- DeviceClass, ResourceClaim,
      ResourceClaimTemplate, ResourceSlice and their full nested type
      graph -- replacing the old v1alpha3-only control-plane-controller
      allocation mode (DRA graduated to GA in Kubernetes v1.34).
      Also added resource.k8s.io/v1beta2 DeviceTaintRule,
      resource.k8s.io/v1alpha3 ResourcePoolStatusRequest,
      scheduling.k8s.io/v1alpha2 PodGroup/Workload (gang scheduling),
      storage.k8s.io/v1 VolumeAttributesClass (GA),
      coordination.k8s.io/v1beta1 LeaseCandidate, and new CSIDriverSpec
      fields (nodeAllocatableUpdatePeriodSeconds,
      preventPodSchedulingIfMissing, serviceAccountTokenInSecrets).
      Fixed a pre-existing bug found while verifying the new DRA classes:
      the api_version group map in IO::K8s::Role::APIObject was missing
      an entry for "resource", so every Api::Resource::* class (both the
      pre-existing v1alpha3 ones and the new ones added here) rendered
      apiVersion as "resource/vX" instead of the correct
      "resource.k8s.io/vX" -- would have produced manifests rejected by
      any real cluster. Fixed by adding resource => 'resource.k8s.io' to
      the map.
      Removed four resource.k8s.io/v1alpha3 classes --
      PodSchedulingContext, PodSchedulingContextSpec,
      PodSchedulingContextStatus, ResourceClaimSchedulingStatus --
      confirmed removed from the live v1.36 API (the "classic DRA"
      control-plane-controller allocation flow they supported was fully
      superseded by the new v1 structured-parameters model). Unlike the
      admission/auth/flowcontrol classes noted above, these had no
      lingering old-cluster back-compat rationale to keep them (DRA
      itself was alpha-only when these shipped, never GA, so there is no
      "still-supported old cluster" using them the way there is for a
      long-GA API's deprecated beta track) -- maintainer confirmed
      removal. Since these names already shipped in IO-K8s 1.100, PAUSE
      redirect tombstones for all four were added to the companion
      IO::K8s::Deprecated distribution rather than left to silently
      orphan.

